{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1554373-draconic-power-how-does-it-work","id":1554373,"title":"Draconic Power - How Does It Work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-15T07:06:21-07:00","id":1554373,"title":"Draconic Power - How Does It Work?","content":"As the title asks, I'm forced to ask myself: &quot;Draconic Power, how does it work?&quot; Because neither Scion: Dragon nor the Dragon Companion that just released to backers actually explain it.<br /> <br /> Draconic Power is apparently the substitute for Inheritance for Tier 4 Heirs aka full Dragons. It's used in place of Inheritance for activating powers, Dragons use it for Divine Realm play, and Dragons begin at Draconic Power 5.<br /> <br /> And that's it. That's all we know about it. We do NOT know what the maximum rating of Draconic Power is. We do NOT know how to increase it, even though that is possible (Scion: Dragon even says that it &quot;starts at 5&quot;, implying upward growth). We don't know anything about the stat which would encourage character growth, like how it works for gaining new Deed names, new Knacks, nothing. And, after double checking the God fundraiser and seeing the stretch goals cover dragons, am I going to have to wait for a third PDF before I or anyone else learns how to actually play as a Dragon? Even though the Kickstarter promised that this companion book would explain how higher level play works?<br /> <br /> Overall, I'm just disappointed that the only thing we got regarding full-on Dragons was material which was already present in the God book and known about for years. It's like someone just wanted to fill out the page count or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T14:06:48-07:00","id":1554493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1554373-draconic-power-how-does-it-work#post1554373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Draconic Power is apparently the substitute for Inheritance for Tier 4 Heirs aka full Dragons. It's used in place of Inheritance for activating powers, Dragons use it for Divine Realm play, and Dragons begin at Draconic Power 5.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Could you give me a page number for that? I can't seem to find it. The only reference to Draconic Power as <i> possible </i> trait is that part under Basic Rules on page 32 of the Companion where it says you can combine it with Legend to generate Effects.<br /> <br /> I don't think we have a section about going from Lesser Wyrm to Greater Wyrm anywhere, beyond the whole Inheritance 10 statement in Scion: Dragon (pg 117). Certainly nothing that explains what that means.<br /> Scion: God 2e says we get those rules in the Dragon Companion, though it says to use Inheritance instead of Legend. If that includes anything beyond the Divine Rule/Realm play, then I don't know where those rules are either.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, you've got all your Spells and Knack slots by Inheritance 9. If Draconic Power is just a renaming thing (unstated, implied) then you would start at Power 10.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T16:20:53-07:00","id":1554499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1554373-draconic-power-how-does-it-work?p=1554493#post1554493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you give me a page number for that? I can't seem to find it. The only reference to Draconic Power as <i> possible </i> trait is that part under Basic Rules on page 32 of the Companion where it says you can combine it with Legend to generate Effects.<br /> <br /> I don't think we have a section about going from Lesser Wyrm to Greater Wyrm anywhere, beyond the whole Inheritance 10 statement in Scion: Dragon (pg 117). Certainly nothing that explains what that means.<br /> Scion: God 2e says we get those rules in the Dragon Companion, though it says to use Inheritance instead of Legend. If that includes anything beyond the Divine Rule/Realm play, then I don't know where those rules are either.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, you've got all your Spells and Knack slots by Inheritance 9. If Draconic Power is just a renaming thing (unstated, implied) then you would start at Power 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pg. 187 in Scion: Dragon, its the small section on Upper-Tier play. It explicitly says that &quot;Dragons replace their Inheritance rating with Draconic Power which starts at 5. Anything that would check for an Inheritance rating now uses Draconic Power. Dragons no longer have Remembrances.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T22:58:20-07:00","id":1554510,"title":"","content":"Thank you. <br /> <br /> Lacking any other information, I'd treat raising Draconic Power like raising Legend or Inheritance. Alternatively you could have it as a complete set; at least one of Worldly (short), Draconic (long), a Brood deed and a Memory Deed. Remember, your Pawn needs to complete the Memory in order to earn the deed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-24T16:58:18-07:00","id":1554653,"title":"","content":"I got a digital copy of the <i>God Player's Guide </i>preview today.<br /> It has a section on this topic on page 15 (but be aware the page indexing could change).<br /> <br /> The Path has spoken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 10-25-2025, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}